  <reporting-org ref="AU-5" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia Aid</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FishTech: Integrating technical fisheries solutions into water development programs in the Mekong</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment builds on a program of ACIAR work which demonstrated that technical solutions mitigate impacts of water infrastructure development on fisheries and provide lasting economic and social benefits for river communities. This investment will upscale, and scale out, adoption of technology that integrates fish passes into existing and new water infrastructure.  From 2022-2025 the program will 1) establish demonstration sites in Laos, Cambodia and Thailand,  2) build capacity on fish passage integration into irrigation programs, 3) support policy development and influence government agencies to mandate developers to better-consider fish passage integration into river development planning and policy,  and 4) facilitate regional engagement and advocacy.</narrative>
  </description>
